GitHub Actions Workflow Validation - 2026-07-18 (Phase 4/5)

VALIDATED ACTION MAJORS:
- actions/checkout@v6
- actions/setup-python@v6 (via setup-python-pipeline composite)
- actions/setup-node@v4 (CI only)
- actions/github-script@v7 (via report-pipeline-failure composite)
- stefanzweifel/git-auto-commit-action@v7

COMPOSITE ACTIONS:
- .github/actions/setup-python-pipeline — setup-python@v6 + pip install requirements.txt; install-dev case-insensitive true (checkout stays in each workflow)
- .github/actions/report-pipeline-failure — ensure pipeline-failure label; Search API by exact title, listForRepo fallback on empty (Search lag); mode=report (default) open/comment, mode=close comment+close (used by weekly-pipeline + live-canary)

WORKFLOWS:
- ci.yml — PR/push; contents:read; npm run verify:fast (lint + pytest not-live + coverage ≥85%)
- weekly-pipeline.yml — schedule + dispatch; contents:write + issues:write; failure → report action; success → commit then close (continue-on-error)
- daily-asx-futures.yml — weekday ASX + meetings refresh; intentionally NO pipeline-failure issues (ASX is optional/lower-severity)
- live-canary.yml — Mon/Thu live pytest; contents:read + issues:write; failure → report action; success → close (continue-on-error)

NOTES:
- npm ci --ignore-scripts in CI (skip local lefthook postinstall)
- data commits use [skip ci] to avoid loops
- critical pipeline failure still refreshes meetings/status (see pipeline/main.py)
- daily ASX silence on issues is intentional — do not add report-pipeline-failure there
- weekly success order is commit then close so Issues API flakiness cannot block data publish

